-- title:
--   A discrete valuation ring along the U-branch of the crossing model
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring which is a domain and a discrete valuation ring, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal, let $\varpi \in W$ be irreducible, and let $e \ge 1$ be a natural number. Write $M =$ `UVCrossingModel W (ϖ ^ e)` for the quotient of the two-variable power series ring $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\,2)\,W$ by the ideal generated by $X_0X_1 - C(\varpi^{e})$, and let $U(\varpi^{e})$, $V(\varpi^{e})$ be its two distinguished elements, whose product is the class $\mathrm{const}(\varpi^{e})(\varpi^{e})$ of the constant $\varpi^{e}$; for $w \in W$, $\mathrm{const}(\varpi^{e})(w)$ denotes the class of the constant power series $C(w)$. The assertion is that there exist a type $D$ carrying the structure of a commutative ring which is a domain and a discrete valuation ring, and a ring homomorphism $\psi : M \to D$, such that: $\psi$ is injective; $\psi(U(\varpi^{e}))$ lies in the maximal ideal of $D$; $\psi(V(\varpi^{e}))$ is a unit of $D$; the maximal ideal of $D$ is the principal ideal generated by $\psi(\mathrm{const}(\varpi^{e})(\varpi))$; and, for every $x \in M$, $\psi(x)$ lies in the maximal ideal of $D$ if and only if $x$ belongs to the ideal of $M$ generated by $U(\varpi^{e})$ and $\mathrm{const}(\varpi^{e})(\varpi)$.
--
--   This realises the localisation of the $A_{e-1}$-type crossing model $W[[U,V]]/(UV-\varpi^{e})$ at the height-one prime $(U,\varpi)$, the generic point of the branch $\{U=0\}$ of the special fibre, as a discrete valuation ring in which $\varpi$ is a uniformiser and $V$ becomes invertible. It is used in the analysis of crossing points of modular curves at full level, where the branch through an end of the special fibre is described by a local parameter.
-- source:
